1
00:00:07,152 --> 00:00:09,734
Whiskers and the Owl of Athens.

2
00:00:20,937 --> 00:00:24,376
One stormy night, Luna was reading Greek myths.

3
00:00:24,576 --> 00:00:28,033
Long ago, Athena and Poseidon both wanted the same city.

4
00:00:33,184 --> 00:00:36,773
Poseidon gave it a spring. But the water was salty. Yuck!

5
00:00:36,973 --> 00:00:41,066
Athena gave it an olive tree. So the city chose her name: Athens!

6
00:00:46,218 --> 00:00:48,196
Is there a myth about dinner?

7
00:00:53,898 --> 00:00:56,641
Hoo! The storm blew me all the way from Athens!

8
00:00:56,841 --> 00:01:01,019
I'm Sophia. My family waits for me on the Parthenon at the full moon.

9
00:01:01,219 --> 00:01:03,013
Easy. I know everything.

10
00:01:03,213 --> 00:01:04,549
Then where is Athens?

11
00:01:04,749 --> 00:01:06,668
South. Mostly. Trust me.

12
00:01:16,770 --> 00:01:22,058
Next morning, a silver airship came humming by, carrying honey to Athens.

13
00:01:22,258 --> 00:01:23,847
Quick! Grab the rope!

14
00:01:31,749 --> 00:01:34,327
Jars of honey? Best. Trip. Ever.

15
00:01:42,229 --> 00:01:48,009
Grandma says Athena's owl was the wisest bird. Not because she knew everything, but because she asked.

16
00:01:48,209 --> 00:01:49,889
Asking is for kittens.

17
00:01:56,691 --> 00:01:58,048
Look! The Acropolis!

18
00:02:03,199 --> 00:02:08,151
But first they had to cross the Plaka: a maze of twisty little streets.

19
00:02:08,351 --> 00:02:10,220
Should we ask somebody the way?

20
00:02:10,420 --> 00:02:12,164
Ask? Never. Follow me.

21
00:02:26,668 --> 00:02:29,123
We've passed this souvlaki stand three times!

22
00:02:29,323 --> 00:02:31,486
On purpose. I like the smell.

23
00:02:36,087 --> 00:02:40,756
Then Whiskers smelled yogurt. Thick white yogurt, with golden honey.

24
00:02:47,558 --> 00:02:49,969
Hoo hoo hoo! He's got a big white beard!

25
00:02:50,169 --> 00:02:53,608
I am a great Greek thinker. And I think... more honey.

26
00:02:59,310 --> 00:03:00,311
Which way now?

27
00:03:00,511 --> 00:03:01,830
Up. Obviously.

28
00:03:06,431 --> 00:03:10,035
Whiskers led them into an ancient stone theatre.

29
00:03:10,235 --> 00:03:11,168
Hello!

30
00:03:14,669 --> 00:03:15,925
I know the way!

31
00:03:18,325 --> 00:03:19,707
No, you don't.

32
00:03:23,208 --> 00:03:25,748
Hey! Echoes aren't supposed to argue!

33
00:03:30,899 --> 00:03:34,170
I'm not an echo. I'm Socrates. And you are lost.

34
00:03:34,370 --> 00:03:36,366
Lost? Us? We're exploring.

35
00:03:39,867 --> 00:03:42,963
The sun was setting. Soon the moon would rise.

36
00:03:43,163 --> 00:03:46,261
My family will be waiting. And I can't fly that high.

37
00:03:51,963 --> 00:03:56,886
Sophia... I don't know the way. I never did. I just wanted to look clever.

38
00:03:57,086 --> 00:04:00,633
The only thing I know is that I know nothing. So I ask.

39
00:04:00,833 --> 00:04:03,453
Like owls! That's why we always say: hoo? Hoo?

40
00:04:06,954 --> 00:04:10,160
Please, Socrates, how do we get to the top?

41
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:13,504
A wise question! Follow the cats of Athens!

42
00:04:21,406 --> 00:04:25,415
Up a secret cat path they climbed, through the olive trees.

43
00:04:31,117 --> 00:04:38,224
Those stone ladies have held up that roof for two thousand years. And I complain about carrying my bowl.

44
00:04:46,126 --> 00:04:47,786
Grandma! I'm home!

45
00:04:54,588 --> 00:04:56,928
Sophia! Thank you, wise cats.

46
00:04:57,128 --> 00:05:00,354
Wise? Me? I didn't know a thing. I just asked.

47
00:05:00,554 --> 00:05:03,422
Little cat, that is how all wisdom begins.

48
00:05:20,126 --> 00:05:22,786
The honey airship carried them home.

49
00:05:27,388 --> 00:05:29,875
An olive tree! And honey! Where have you been?

50
00:05:30,075 --> 00:05:34,339
Athens, Pip! Ask me anything. If I don't know, we'll ask together.

51
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:45,447
Because nobody knows everything. And the wisest words of all are: let's ask!

